  "project_description": "Splunk Real User Monitoring (RUM) pinpoints issues that impact customers with end-to-end visibility from browser or mobile app to backend services. This is a part of the Splunk Observability Cloud solution.\n\n Features \n The module provides a configuration interface to add an accesstoken, application name and environment to add properties to the SignalFX javascript.\n\n Post-Installation \n Install the module like always. Go to /admin/config/splunk-rum and add the required parameters. Save, and the script is added. \n\n Additional Requirements \n This only works if you have an up and running Splunk Observability environment.\n\n Recommended modules/libraries \n - OpenTelemetry \n\n Please note that if you get \"Unhandled export error\" in OpenTelemetry, you should try the following solution:\n\n https://www.drupal.org/project/opentelemetry/issues/3416011#comment-154… \n\n Back to top",
